{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01340",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.81,
      "end_seconds": 7.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.63,
      "end_seconds": 13.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.16,
      "end_seconds": 22.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Mainly a stiff painful shoulder. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.95,
      "end_seconds": 29.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.34,
      "end_seconds": 35.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "It's been five days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.61,
      "end_seconds": 39.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Okay, go on. How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.62,
      "end_seconds": 41.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.3,
      "end_seconds": 46.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.51,
      "end_seconds": 63.89,
      "duration_seconds": 16.38,
      "text": "It usually comes with not being able to lift my arm. The not being able to lift my arm? That's been since yesterday. As for not being able to lift my arm, moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.84,
      "end_seconds": 70.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Okay, any neck pain, fall or numbness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.24,
      "end_seconds": 74.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Erm, nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.09,
      "end_seconds": 79.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.24,
      "end_seconds": 83.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.73,
      "end_seconds": 87.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.91,
      "end_seconds": 93.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I had a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.82,
      "end_seconds": 114.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.86,
      "end_seconds": 120.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster tramadol gave me vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.94,
      "end_seconds": 136.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.61,
      "end_seconds": 141.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.03,
      "end_seconds": 158.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.67,
      "end_seconds": 180.53,
      "duration_seconds": 20.86,
      "text": "I'm on gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day. Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day. I'm on ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, when needed. I took the morning off to come in today. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.39,
      "end_seconds": 185.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.4,
      "end_seconds": 197.82,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 199.74,
      "end_seconds": 210.89,
      "duration_seconds": 11.15,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temperature 36.6, pulse is 78 beats a minute. Blood pressure 111 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.0,
      "end_seconds": 212.7,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.93,
      "end_seconds": 217.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.04,
      "end_seconds": 220.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.22,
      "end_seconds": 239.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Movement is limited in all directions, both active and passive."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.37,
      "end_seconds": 253.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like adhesive capsulitis, a frozen shoulder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.08,
      "end_seconds": 290.1,
      "duration_seconds": 23.02,
      "text": "We should do an X-ray of the shoulder for shoulder pain. Gentle daily stretches within comfort, and heat before them. I'll also refer you to physiotherapy. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. Let's plan a check in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.65,
      "end_seconds": 292.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "That's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.14,
      "end_seconds": 296.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.63,
      "end_seconds": 299.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.69,
      "end_seconds": 301.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}